From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:35:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] drm/panfrost: Unmask the interrupts of a re-enabled
 address space

Sashiko reported this in a review of an unrelated patch.

After an unhandled page fault, the address space is added to
as_faulty_mask, its MMU is disabled, and the IRQ thread unmasks every
interrupt but the ones of that AS. panfrost_mmu_as_get() re-enables the
AS for the next job, but it writes ~as_faulty_mask to MMU_INT_MASK
before it removes the AS from as_faulty_mask, so the interrupts of the
AS stay masked. The next fault on it, a heap growth fault for example,
raises no interrupt, and the job hangs until the scheduler timeout
resets the GPU.

Remove the AS from as_faulty_mask before writing the mask.

Fixes: ed7a34c57def ("drm/panfrost: Disable the AS on unhandled page faults")
Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260811215454.A1C8D1F000E9@smtp.kernel.org/
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
index 70fa751..289cbac 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_mmu.c
@@ -283,9 +283,9 @@ int panfrost_mmu_as_get(struct panfrost_device *pfdev, struct panfrost_mmu *mmu)
 			 * disabled. We need to re-enable the MMU after
 			 * clearing+unmasking the AS interrupts.
 			 */
+			pfdev->as_faulty_mask &= ~mask;
 			mmu_write(pfdev, MMU_INT_CLEAR, mask);
 			mmu_write(pfdev, MMU_INT_MASK, ~pfdev->as_faulty_mask);
-			pfdev->as_faulty_mask &= ~mask;
 			panfrost_mmu_enable(pfdev, mmu);
 		}
 
